<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Cue is not sandboxed: it is distributed directly, so the sandbox would buy
  nothing here. The hardened runtime is still applied at signing time because
  notarization requires it, and it blocks nothing this app does.

  No Accessibility, no Screen Recording, no Full Disk Access, no Input
  Monitoring. The global shortcut is a registered hotkey rather than an event
  tap: the window server tells Cue when its own combination is pressed and shows
  it nothing else, so there is nothing to grant. The only things Cue talks to
  are Google's own hosts, and only after you sign in.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
